d DATALIB: UNICEF Microdata Library - Data Loading and Processing Utility
d Version 0.9.19
d Author: Joao Pedro Azevedo (jpazevedo@unicef.org)
d Date: 2026-07-26
d
d Description:
d   DATALIB is a comprehensive utility designed to facilitate the loading,
d   processing, and merging of survey data modules across different countries
d   and years. It provides a user-friendly interface for navigating the data
d   repository, selecting specific surveys, and performing data operations.
d   When certain parameters like country, year, or survey are not specified,
d   DATALIB launches an interactive navigation mode to help users browse
d   available options.
d
d Features:
d   - Interactive folder navigation through data repository (_foldernav)
d   - Data loading and processing utilities (_dlw)
d   - Directory structure creation and management (_mkdir)
d   - Country, survey, vintage, and adaptation verification functions
d   - Contract v1 datalib_* API (resolve, catalog, enumerate, load, create)
d     shared with the R and Python implementations (see help datalib_api)
d
d Organization:
d   Files are organized alphabetically by initial letter in subdirectories:
d   src/d/ - the datalib command and the datalib_* contract wrappers
d   src/g/ - getuserconfig user-config loader
d   src/m/ - mapzdrive network drive mapper
d   src/_/ - All utility functions starting with underscore
d
d Installation:
d   From a clone of the (private) repository:
d   net install datalib, from("<path-to-clone>/stata") replace
d
d Keywords: survey, data, microdata, utility, navigation
d
